@c Current guidance for the built-in Emacs Term integration.
@node Running Terminal Based Applications
@chapter Term Terminal Access

@cindex Term mode
@cindex terminal applications
@cindex Eterm, Emacsvox module name

Emacsvox speech-enables the built-in Emacs Term terminal emulator through the
module named @code{emacsvox-eterm}.  The module name is inherited; users do not
install a separate Eterm package.

For a new full-terminal workflow, prefer @ref{EAT Terminal Access}.  EAT has
the richer current guide for bounded screen output, terminal-side completion,
scrollback, alternate screens, and asynchronous rendering.  Use built-in Term
when avoiding an additional package matters or an application specifically
works better there.  For ordinary line-oriented shell commands, @kbd{M-x
shell} is usually simpler than either terminal emulator.

